> and ko'e in {ko'a nau ca'a xanka ko'e ko'i}. You are saying that as
> long as ko'i does not obtain, we don't claim that ko'e is actually
> making ko'a nervous at all. It's just the potentiality of her being
> nervous that is claimed to be actual and current.
>

  By the way, if we know that the terxanka  is  true, then  the  nervousnes=
s
is actual, not potential:
"la meris ba klama lo mikce .i la meris xanka lo za'i selkenra  kei lo nu
go'i" (Mary is going to the doctor.  Mary is nervous about having cancer
BECAUSE of this).
is functionally equivalent in meaning to "la meris xanka lo za'i selkenra
.iki'ubo my ba klama lo mikce" -> (Mary is nervous about having cancer
BECAUSE she will be going the doctor.)
